{"kind":"promise","text":"Fresh promise on the replacement assignment. I will re-anchor twelve pages now and defer three, semantically rather than by substitution.\n\nI will honour the constraint that matters most in this version: repairing a dependency edge is not the same as the page being current, and I will not let the artifact or the report imply it is. Every anchor I choose will be world-stale, because every artifact at the packages these pages describe is world-stale, so the docs artifact will flare from birth. That is the correct outcome and I will say so plainly rather than presenting a green record.\n\nWhat semantically means here, so it is judgeable. For each page I read what it claims about behaviour and pick the shipped path that carries that claim. gs supersede's page is about staleness propagation, which lives in internal/workroom, not in the command surface; gs status's page is about the projection; docs/concepts/staleness.md, docs/anchoring.md and docs/why.md are fold behaviour throughout. Where a page genuinely describes the command surface rather than the semantics behind it, cmd/gs/main.go is the honest anchor. I will not reuse the successor mapping from my survey: it was a list of what broke, and several of its entries would move a page between paths that do not carry its subject.\n\nThe bootstrap note cites b739ae18, which resolves to no event. I will find what its claims actually rest on and cite that, or remove the citation and say the note rests on nothing durable. I will not substitute a plausible-looking artifact to make the front matter parse.\n\nDeferred: docs/how-to/configure-an-agent.md and docs/reference/mcp/status.md and wait.md, until the addressed-inbox work lands. fa7c9b73 is still unmerged and its artifacts are stale, so anchoring them now would cite a moving branch.\n\nOne exact head on request/docs-behavior-reanchor, one docs artifact resting on this request, this promise, and every behaviour artifact I select, make docs and gi